# cuttle-stealth-chromium patch #06 - navigator.{platform,userAgent,
# hardwareConcurrency} from --fingerprint-platform / -hardware-concurrency.
#
# These are placed on NavigatorBase (not NavigatorID or
# NavigatorConcurrentHardware) because that is the JS-visible entry point;
# the more-specific classes are short-circuited by NavigatorBase before
# reaching them. WorkerNavigator inherits it, so workers see the same values.
#
# navigator.userAgent carries no version literal. Its major comes from
# --fingerprint-brand-version through cuttle::seed::BrandVersion(), the value
# patch 0007 builds UA-CH from, so a malformed value is dropped on both alike;
# the fallback is the version the browser puts in the UA metadata
# (version_info). It is emitted in the reduced major.0.0.0 form, the same form
# cuttle's --user-agent carries, so the page string equals the HTTP User-Agent
# header byte for byte.
#
# Source: chromium 154.0.8037.57
#   third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/navigator_base.cc
